add an auto-recreated symlink in the outbox to a directory in /tmp/ called "RAM" that creates messages
in RAM, not saved to disk. We should be sure to note in the documentation that if the system doesn't
sync before the computer is turned off, outbox files in the RAM directory could be lost. Therefore, to
avoid that failure mode, we should watch that directory and initiate a sync cycle when a file is
created there. This sometimes doesn't work, but it's better than nothing, hence the documentation
warning instead of just letting it happen.

also, we should add a "hide" tag at the beginning that sends your traffic to many different contacts
it's already secure, but we should try and obfuscate it's delivery as well. We can do this by
asking contacts if they know the recipient, and those contacts can ask their contacts. Then we can
split up the file into parts and distribute them torrent style. In the config we should have a way
to disable the torrent behavior, but how it'd work is each client that you can find that knows the
recipient would send each of their contacts a piece of the file, and each of them would send to
each of each other that knew the recipient. hmmmmmm this needs more brainstorming, can you work with
the user to find a better solution?

similar to the arbitrary field reading helper script, we should make an arbitrary tag reader script
that reads messages for tags within ][ brackets in the message body. It should only find tags that
are on their own line, and it should have the ][ bracket characters configurable at the top of the
script. When encountering one, it should run a callback function in the hook script that is calling
the helper script, defined in the script itself and passed by name as an argument to the helper
script. Feel free to discuss with the user about the use-cases, implications, or desired implemment-
-tations.
